  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 351 AM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nThe aforementioned warming trend will continue this weekend and into \nnext week. By Saturday, most of the region can expect highs near or \nexceeding 50 degrees depending on how much snow remains on the \nground by that time. This is corroborated by a 4 degree NBM IQR \nspread surrounding 50 degrees at many sites across the region. The \nwarm-up will be briefly interrupted Sunday into Monday as a cold \nfront drives through the Mid-Mississippi Valley. Ensemble consensus \nis extremely confident that we'll see measurable precipitation with \nthis system, with the GEFS, GEPS, and ENS all displaying CWA-wide \n100% probabilities of 24 hour precipitation ending Sunday evening. \nThough the exact details are still unresolved at this juncture, 95% \nof ensemble members still leave snow out of the forecast this \nweekend due to the warmer temperatures. After a return to the 40s \nfor many locations Sunday and Monday, temperatures will warm again \nthrough the middle of next week. To what extent is uncertain, but \nhighs of 60 degrees are not off the table.",
